voidfabricator.tooltip.block.header=[AE-Native Virtual Crafting]
voidfabricator.tooltip.block.description.1=Reads machine recipe pools from up to 27 physical patterns and publishes processing patterns to AE.
voidfabricator.tooltip.block.description.2=Order from any normal AE Crafting Terminal; no block-side ordering GUI is needed.
voidfabricator.tooltip.block.requirement=Requires an online AE network with at least one standard Crafting CPU.
voidfabricator.tooltip.block.no_private_cpu=Registers no private CPU and adds no extra entry to the CPU list.
voidfabricator.tooltip.block.consumption=Consumes only real inputs delivered by AE; never runs the GT machine or charges twice.
voidfabricator.tooltip.block.energy=Power: one debit from the block owner's GT wireless EU grid at recipe EU/t × duration × batches; the balance is checked first and the craft is rejected if it is insufficient.
voidfabricator.tooltip.block.buffer=Outputs enter a persistent buffer, survive disconnects, and retry after reconnection.
voidfabricator.tooltip.block.speed=No GT processing duration; actual throughput still depends on AE scheduling and server load.
voidfabricator.tooltip.block.install=Install: empty-hand right-click opens the block panel. A normal right-click with the pattern opens the pattern's own center; sneak-right-click the block to install it into the block slot.
voidfabricator.tooltip.block.status=Empty-hand right-click opens the panel with published pattern count, pending batches, filtered recipes, and AE connection state.
voidfabricator.tooltip.block.protection=Normal breaking and explosions are blocked while accepted outputs remain undelivered.
voidfabricator.tooltip.block.advanced=Advanced: output buffer limit is 256 pending batches and 512 stack entries.

